          %h3#the_cartesian_lifts The cartesian lifts
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            has
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi cod
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi I
                  %mo ,
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cod : [I,C] \to C
            is in addition a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+fibration"} fibered category
            in the sense of Grothendieck:
          %p
            for every object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi c
